    "created_at": "2018-06-08T15:21:33Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-06-08T15:21:33Z",
    "body": "I think it would be wonderful to have a \"inherit stuff\" algorithm that brought forward origin, service worker controller, etc.  Maybe it would include stuff like CSP as well, etc.  Then specs could just be written to \"inherit stuff\" and it would get everything.\r\n\r\nThe question is, do we currently inherit everything consistently today?  And if we don't, can we align them all to inherit consistently?\r\n\r\nThis definitely seems like a bigger set of refactoring to the spec, though.",
